    "id": "anamorphic",
    "name": "Anamorphic Illusion",
    "description": "A bright pale gallery room where dozens of chunky painted rods hang on thin strings at very different depths: meaningless clutter from every angle except one sweet spot (a taped cross on the floor), where every piece lines up into one crisp word or shape. Each piece is a slice of the figure moved along its own eye ray and scaled with distance, so from the sweet spot the figure is exact and from a few degrees off parallax tears it apart. Two figures can share one room (each with its own sweet spot and colour); the figure not being read sinks to its own muted mid-tone. Soft cast shadows on the floor and walls show the true scatter even at the locked moment.",
